.TH MELOS 1 "2026-11-19" "melos 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
melos \- fast, minimal terminal music player for local files and YouTube downloads
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B melos
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B melos
.B status
.br
.B melos
.B stop
.br
.B melos
.B import
[\fB\-\-copy\fR] \fIPATH\fR...
.br
.B melos
.B scan
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B melos
is a terminal music player. It connects to the resident
.BR melosd (1)
daemon, starting it on demand, and displays a keyboard-driven interface for the
library, playlists, queue, downloads, lyrics, and listening statistics. Local
folders and audio files can be indexed where they are or copied into the
managed library. The selected track's cover art appears in the sidebar when the
file has embedded art or a nearby cover image. Lyrics are fetched from LRCLIB
and can be pasted or edited manually.
.PP
The daemon owns playback and continues when the client exits. Press
.B q
to detach and leave music playing, or
.B Q
to stop playback and shut the daemon down.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
Read configuration from
.IR PATH
instead of
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/melos/config.toml .
.TP
.B \-\-trace\-startup
Print first-frame and connection timings to standard error after the interface
exits.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Print whether the daemon is running, the library and queue size, and the
current track.
.TP
.B stop
Ask the daemon to stop playback and exit.
.TP
.BI import " [\-\-copy] " PATH ...
Add folders or individual audio files to the library. Without
.B \-\-copy
the originals are indexed in place; with it they are copied into
.IR ~/Music/melos/Imported .
.TP
.B scan
Rescan every active music source.
.SH KEY BINDINGS
Navigation accepts both vim keys and the usual arrow keys.
.TP
.B j k, Down Up
Move the selection down or up.
.TP
.B g G, Home End
Jump to the first or last item.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+d ", " Ctrl+u ", " PgDn ", " PgUp
Move by half a page or a full page.
.TP
.B Tab
Switch between the sidebar and the main pane.
.TP
.BR 1 " " 2 " " 3 " " 4 " " 5 " " 6
Open Library, Playlists, Queue, Downloads, Lyrics, or Statistics. Opening
Library, a playlist, or the queue moves the cursor to the currently playing
track.
.TP
.B I
Open the music sources overlay. Use
.B a
to add a folder or file,
.B d
to forget the selected source,
.B Enter
to rescan it, and
.B R
to rescan every active source. Forgetting never deletes files.
.TP
.B R
Rescan every active music source.
.TP
.B Enter
Play the selected track, open a playlist, confirm an input, or seek to the
selected or current lyric line in the Lyrics pane.
.TP
.B Space
Pause or resume.
.TP
.B n p
Next or previous track.
.TP
.B Left Right
Seek backward or forward five seconds.
.TP
.B Shift+Left Shift+Right
Seek backward or forward thirty seconds.
.TP
.B + \-
Change the volume.
.TP
.B m
Toggle mute.
.TP
.B s
Toggle shuffle.
.TP
.B r
Cycle repeat mode.
.TP
.B a
Add the selected track to the queue.
.TP
.B A
Add the selected track to a playlist.
.TP
.B V
Start or end visual selection in the Library, a playlist, or the queue. Use
.B j
and
.B k
to extend the selection.
.TP
.B J K
Move the selected block down or up one position. The Library and playlists keep
this order across restarts; the queue moves the block without changing which
track is playing.
.TP
.B N
Create a playlist.
.TP
.B d
Remove the selected item from the queue or playlist, cancel the selected
download, or open the removal dialog on a Library track.
.TP
.B Delete
Remove the selected track from the library. A dialog chooses between forgetting
the track in melos only and deleting the audio file as well. File deletion is
allowed only inside the managed library or an active source.
.TP
.BR e ", " F2
Rename the selected playlist or track. This changes melos' display name only;
audio tags and filenames are not modified.
.TP
.BR p ", " P
Paste lyrics in the Lyrics pane. LRC timestamps are detected automatically;
plain text is saved as unsynced lyrics. Press Ctrl+S to save.
.TP
.BR e ", " E
Open the current lyrics in
.IR $EDITOR .
.TP
.BR f ", " F
Refetch lyrics from LRCLIB.
.TP
.B [ ]
Shift lyric synchronization by half a second.
.TP
.BR j ", " k
Select the next or previous line in synced lyrics, or scroll plain lyrics.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+d ", " Ctrl+u
Move the synced selection or scroll plain lyrics by half a page in the Lyrics
pane.
.TP
.BR PgUp ", " PgDn
Move the synced selection or scroll plain lyrics by a full page in the Lyrics
pane.
.TP
.B Enter
Seek to the selected synced lyric line.
.TP
.B Esc
Exit visual selection, or return synced lyrics to following playback after
selecting a line.
.TP
.B i
Download: enter a search query or a YouTube URL.
.TP
.B /
Filter the current list.
.TP
.B ?
Show the help overlay.
.TP
.BR q ", " Ctrl+c
Detach from the daemon; playback continues.
.TP
.B Q
Stop playback and shut down the daemon.
.TP
.B Esc
Cancel the current input or close an overlay.
.PP
Bindings can be changed in
.IR config.toml ;
the help overlay reflects the active keymap.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/melos/config.toml
Configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/melos/library.db
SQLite index of tracks, sources, playlists, lyrics, and statistics.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/melos/state.json
Queue, position, volume, shuffle, and repeat state.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/melos/art
Extracted cover art cache.
.TP
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR /melos/daemon.sock
Unix socket used by the client.
.TP
.I ~/Music/melos
Managed library for downloads and copied imports.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory for the configuration.
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Base directory for the library index.
.TP
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
Base directory for persistent player state and logs.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Base directory for extracted cover art.
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Base directory for the client socket. Falls back to
.IR /tmp/melos\-UID .
.TP
.B MELOS_ART
Select the artwork renderer.
.B auto
(the default) uses native Kitty graphics in Kitty and a colored half-block
rendering elsewhere.
.B halfblocks
forces the fallback.
.B kitty
forces Kitty graphics.
.SH EXAMPLES
Open the player:
.PP
.nf
.RS
melos
.RE
.fi
.PP
Check what is playing without opening the interface:
.PP
.nf
.RS
melos status
.RE
.fi
.PP
Index a folder in place, then copy another folder into the managed library:
.PP
.nf
.RS
melos import ~/Music/Albums
melos import --copy ~/Downloads/New\\ Album
.RE
.fi
.PP
Stop playback and the daemon:
.PP
.nf
.RS
melos stop
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR melosd (1),
.BR mpv (1),
.BR yt\-dlp (1),
.BR playerctl (1)
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at https://github.com/ZT-Things/melos/issues.
